! The displaced silicon of si2-nc-force.in with an ultrasoft pseudopotential.
!
! What this case adds is the augmentation charge's own contribution to the force:
! Q_ij(r - tau) moves with the atom, so the density does too even at fixed
! wavefunctions, and the overlap operator S makes the orthonormality constraint
! position-dependent as well (QE's `addusforce` and the eps-weighted half of
! `force_us`). A norm-conserving force has neither term.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
    tprnfor = .true.
    verbosity = 'high'
 /
 &system
    ibrav=2, celldm(1)=10.20, nat=2, ntyp=1,
    ecutwfc=20.0, ecutrho=160.0
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-10
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Si  28.086  Si.pz-n-rrkjus_psl.0.1.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (alat)
 Si 0.00 0.00 0.00
 Si 0.27 0.25 0.25
K_POINTS (automatic)
 4 4 4 0 0 0
